  "id": "Compound::DB00535 - Gene::6565",
  "verbalization": "Cefdinir, a cephalosporin antibiotic, is consistently linked to Slc15a2 through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Cefdinir, as part of the cephalosporin class, binds to Slc15a2, a transporter involved in nutrient uptake. This relationship is supported by multiple paths, including direct interactions between Cefdinir and Slc15a2, as well as indirect pathways through other cephalosporins like cefotaxime and cefepime. The lowest common ancestors across these paths indicate a shared classification within the cephalosporin family, reinforcing the biological relevance of the interaction. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition of Slc15a2, which may disrupt cellular homeostasis, potentially contributing to adverse effects such as dermatitis. The integration of these pathways highlights a consistent, mechanistically plausible link between Cefdinir and Slc15a2, supported by both direct and indirect evidence.",
